          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "A useful distinction is emerging. The earlier safe-line counterexample lets source bounds worsen as a prime grows. I’m checking a fixed-prime family instead: it keeps common source and zero-count bounds, while a perturbation of order \\(d^2\\) creates a Green signal of order \\(d\\). If this calculation holds, it gives a precise conditioning limit for the proposed resolvent method, while leaving estimates specific to the unchanged theta source open.\n"
            ]
          },
